WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Type I covers small appliances. Don't underestimate this section — it has tricky
questions.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Self-contained recovery equipment has its own compressor and can recover
refrigerant regardless of whether the appliance compressor works. It connects to
the system through access valves or process tubes. The recovered refrigerant

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Process Tube: A sealed copper tube on a small appliance that can be pierced for
access to the refrigerant circuit.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Access Valve: A valve installed on the system to allow gauge and recovery
equipment connection.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Self-contained recovery is the more reliable
method since it does not depend on the appliance working.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Equipment must be EPA-certified. And — Recovery cylinders
must be DOT-approved

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
What is the maximum charge that defines a small appliance under EPA 608? That
number is on the exam.

